    "done_when": "§11 asks for the producer's CPU over the measured nine-worker shape, read with pidstat for 60 s, before and after. The measured baseline is 60 to 66 percent of a core on 2026-09-24. Both arms run on the fleet allocation in a temporary RECKON_HOME, never against the live reckon producer or ~/.config/reckon. A driver synthesises nine live run pointers whose stream.jsonl files each grow at a steady rate of about 2 MB over the window, using realistic assistant and tool records. It runs `reckon crew watch` for the project as the producer, once from a git archive extraction of 42eddfe1782a6a4bb3e5021f518304d00068e526 (the parent of the §11 merge bebae5a7a) and once from current main. For each arm it reads pidstat -u 1 60 on the producer's own process id (or utime+stime deltas from that process's /proc stat file when pidstat is absent) and records mean and peak %CPU. It also records 8 s of strace -c -f read/openat counts where strace is available, the revision each arm imported (asserted from module __file__), the growth rate and the run count. A report producer-cpu.md in the run directory, copied to ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/, states both figures and the ratio; the driver, both logs and the pidstat outputs stay in the run directory. Every producer the driver started is stopped by pid and listed, and none outlives the node.",
    "estimated_hours": 1.0,
    "goal": "The producer's CPU over a nine-run shape is measured before and after incremental stream reads",
